Where Qwen Lives & How the App Accesses ItNo Heavy Local Model Bloat: We do not force a 1.1 GB–1.6 GB model into the base .apk or PWA download, which would crash 2 GB–4 GB RAM Pakistani Android phones and violate fast load times.Stateless Cloudflare Worker Proxy (tibb-ai-gateway.workers.dev):When the device is online and the patient is in a Green (Home Care) or Amber (Clinic Visit) state, the app sends only de-identified clinical state variables (e.g., { ageBracket: "2-5y", gender: "M", triageTier: "GREEN", primarySymptom: "mild_fever", language: "ur" }) to our Cloudflare Worker.Zero API Key Exposure: Your inference API keys live inside Cloudflare Worker Secrets—never inside the React frontend or APK.Multi-Provider Free-Tier Cascade: The Worker routes requests to Groq Free Tier (qwen/qwen3-32b or qwen-2.5-32b at ~30 RPM / 1,000 RPD), automatically failing over to Hugging Face Inference Providers (Qwen/Qwen2.5-7B-Instruct) or OpenRouter :free endpoints if a 429 Rate Limit occurs.Instant Offline / Red-Flag Bypass: If navigator.onLine === false, if the request takes $> 3.5\text{ seconds}$, or if any Red-Flag danger sign is triggered, Tibb skips Qwen completely and renders verified, pre-bundled trilingual WHO clinical guidance in $< 15\text{ milliseconds}$.2. Rigorous Clinical Safety, Unbiased Guardrails & Verification PipelineTo satisfy medical judges and Pakistan regulatory boundaries (DRAP Medical Devices Rules & Pakistan National Action Plan on AMR), every single output passes through a 4-Gate Clinical Safety Pipeline before the patient ever sees a word:Gate 1: Mandatory Structured Intake (Before Any Guidance)Whenever a new Care Episode starts, Tibb enforces structured context collection—just like a physician—using zero-typing tap cards:Patient Profile: Age (exact months for infants $<2\text{ yrs}$, years for children/adults), biological sex, pregnancy/lactation flag (for females $12\text{–}55\text{ yrs}$), and known chronic conditions (Diabetes, Hypertension, Asthma, Heart Disease) or drug allergies.Current Episode Vitals & Signs: Duration of symptoms, temperature band (Normal / Mild Fever / High Fever), hydration status, and optional emergency vitals (60-second breathing tap-count or camera pulse estimate).Gate 2: Deterministic Red-Flag Circuit Breaker (Hardcoded TypeScript)Before any AI or home-care logic runs, a pure function evaluateRedFlags(episode) checks WHO IMCI (pediatric) and WHO ETAT/IITT (adult) danger signs:Pediatric Danger Signs: Unable to drink/breastfeed, vomits everything, convulsions/fits, lethargic/unconscious, chest indrawing, stridor in calm child, or fast breathing ($\ge 60\text{ bpm}$ for $<2\text{ mo}$; $\ge 50\text{ bpm}$ for $2\text{–}11\text{ mo}$; $\ge 40\text{ bpm}$ for $12\text{ mo–}5\text{ yr}$).Adult Danger Signs: Crushing chest pain/pressure, sudden unilateral weakness/slurred speech (FAST stroke), severe shortness of breath, uncontrolled bleeding, altered mental status, or fever with stiff neck/petechial rash.Action on Trigger: Immediately locks the UI into RED EMERGENCY OVERRIDE, suppresses all home remedies and LLM chat, sounds an alert chime, displays 1-tap emergency dial buttons (1122 Rescue, 115 Edhi, 1020 Chhipa, 1166 Sehat Tahaffuz), and routes to the nearest pre-cached tertiary hospital (e.g., PIMS, Polyclinic, Holy Family) with a 1-tap QR Referral Slip.Gate 3: Zero-Prescription Policy & Controlled Home-Care MatrixAbsolute Prescription Ban: Tibb never recommends, names, or calculates dosages for antibiotics (Amoxicillin, Azithromycin, Ciprofloxacin, etc.), steroids, sedatives, or prescription pharmaceuticals.Evidence-Based Supportive Home Care (Green Tier Only): For verified Green episodes with zero red flags, Tibb provides strictly vetted WHO Supportive Comfort Measures (e.g., WHO low-osmolarity ORS preparation ratios for mild diarrhea, tepid sponging and fluid intake for mild fever, honey/warm fluids for cough in children $>1\text{ year}$—explicitly blocking honey for infants $<12\text{ months}$ to prevent infant botulism).Mandatory Escalation Trigger: Every supportive home-care card includes an explicit "When to Stop Home Care & See a Doctor" timer (e.g., "If fever lasts $>48\text{ hours}$ or breathing becomes fast, visit your nearest BHU immediately").Gate 4: Pre-Display Output Auditor & Anti-Bias GuardrailEvery response returned from Qwen passes through a synchronous TypeScript sanitizer (auditClinicalOutput()) before rendering:DRAP / WHO AWaRe Regex Blocker: Scans output against a list of 180+ generic and Pakistani brand drug names (e.g., Augmentin, Flagyl, Panadol dosages, Brufen dosages). If detected, the entire LLM response is discarded and replaced with a verified deterministic template.Diagnostic Phrase Blocker: Strips absolute diagnostic claims ("You have typhoid", "This is pneumonia") and enforces probabilistic triage framing ("These signs require evaluation for...").Demographic Bias Audit: System prompts explicitly prohibit differential pain or urgency discounting based on gender, rural/urban district, or socioeconomic status. Triage severity is computed exclusively by deterministic physiological rules, never by Qwen.3. Complete Feature Matrix (Multimodal, Vitals, Alarms & Reports)FeatureHow It Works (Online + Offline)Technical Implementation1. Emergency Vital Estimators (Zero-Hardware)A. 60-Second WHO Breath & Pulse Tap-Timer: User taps screen with each breath or radial/carotid pulse beat; app computes exact BPM and compares against WHO age-adjusted thresholds.B. Smartphone Camera rPPG Pulse Estimator (Experimental Screen): User places fingertip gently over rear camera + flash for 20 seconds; extracts green-channel photoplethysmography (PPG) waveform peaks to estimate resting heart rate (labelled clearly as "Wellness/Triage Estimate — Confirm with Medical Device").C. Non-Measurable Vitals (BP & Blood Sugar): Never faked via camera (pseudoscientific and unsafe). Instead, Tibb provides rapid symptom-proxy screening (e.g., polyuria/p